SECURE. #C914 stack-dispatch-at-tip on e01271e5. A stack-ready note only releases a hold: the note text is ignored, and only the annotated sha is read, regex-checked to 40 hex. A forged or stray note means an early review, which is today's behavior; a hold never skips the ship gate's signatures. Cards with a review note or findings are never held. The schema allows stack {hold:true, branch?} only: no tip, tipSha, size or outside, and branch is regex-checked. compat-view drops a hold, so neither the hold nor its branch reaches the page. stack-ready.mjs uses execFileSync git with fixed arrays and no shell. LOW: it pushes HEAD from any branch, main included, and flight-board's pre-push hook does not guard main; refusing main (and the default branch) would close that mistake path.
